{/* Two centred bars of the same length, cut square at both ends — the filter
    mark reduced to what it means. Square viewBox so the glyph sits in the
    middle of a round pill rather than filling it edge to edge.

    `stroke-linecap` is `butt` rather than the `round` this had: the ends stop
    flat, exactly on the coordinate the path names, so both bars measure the
    same 16 and neither gains a half-stroke cap at either end. */}
<svg
  class="filter-lines"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  fill="none"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  stroke-width="2"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
  <path d="M4 9h16"></path>
  <path d="M4 15h16"></path>
</svg>
